<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Pope Pius VII</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1742">1742</a>–<a href="/years/1823">1823</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/18th-century">18th century</a> · Also known as Barnaba Chiaramonti</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Pius VII, born Barnaba Chiaramonti, was pope from 1800 to 1823. He concluded the Concordat of 1801 with <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/napoleon">Napoleon</a> and attended his coronation in 1804, but after Napoleon annexed the Papal States in 1809 he was held captive in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/france">France</a> until 1814. The <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/congress-of-vienna">Congress of Vienna</a> restored the Papal States to him.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/pope-pius-vii.jpg" alt="Pope Pius VII" width="320" height="493" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Thomas Lawrence · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Sir_Thomas_Lawrence_-_Portrait_of_Pope_Pius_VII.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
